-- host.lua -- machine-specific Hyprland settings.
--
-- Copy to ~/.config/hypr/host.lua and edit. NOT tracked by this repo and NOT
-- linked by install.sh: it is the one file that is meant to differ per machine,
-- which is exactly what should not be shared between them.
--
-- hyprland.lua loads it with pcall(dofile, ...) before anything else, so it can
-- set globals the rest of the config reads -- WSBANDS in particular.
--
-- Hyprland's autoreload watches the config files it parses itself. This one is
-- reached through dofile and is not among them, so a change here lands with
-- `hyprctl reload` (or the next login) and not on save.
--
-- Find your monitor names and ids with:  hyprctl monitors

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Monitors
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- hl.monitor({ output = "DP-3",     mode = "preferred", position = "auto", scale = "auto" })
-- hl.monitor({ output = "HDMI-A-1", mode = "preferred", position = "auto", scale = "auto",
--              transform = 1 })  -- 1 = 90 degrees, i.e. portrait

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Lid, on a laptop
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- logind suspends on a lid close only while nothing else is attached: a second
-- connected display counts as docked, and HandleLidSwitchDocked defaults to
-- ignore. So on a docked laptop the switch reaches nothing, and the built-in
-- panel stays lit -- windows and all -- under a shut lid. Disable it instead.
--
-- Three things this has to get right, all measured 2026-08-26:
--
--   * hl.monitor() applies at runtime, from a bind callback. `hyprctl keyword
--     monitor` does not -- under a Lua config it refuses with "keyword can't
--     work with non-legacy parsers".
--   * re-applying a spec that merely omits `disabled` does NOT clear an earlier
--     disable. The key has to be present and false.
--   * a switch bind fires on a transition only, so a login or a reload with the
--     lid already shut needs the state reconciling once by hand.
--
-- `locked = true` is what `bindl` means in hyprland.conf syntax: the bind has to
-- fire with the lockscreen up, which is exactly when the lid is shut.

